/* lower and upper case substitution tables. Codepage 850 Latin-I. Initiated 2.4.1a, extended 2.8.0

   Putting these arrays into agnhlps.c sometimes provoked compilation errors. Also, according to a
   posting at StackOverflow, it had put the substitution lookup arrays on the stack every time the
   functions using them had been called, since `extern` cannot be mixed with `static` declarations.
   See StackOverflow article `A tutorial on lookup tables in C` by Nigel Jones. */

